.TH "SKOGAI MEMORY" 1  "skogai memory 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai memory \- memory: one fact per file, each with a stale_after; expired ones get decided on
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai memory\fR <COMMAND>
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
skogai memory\-ls(1)
every entry: stale_after, name, description; `!` marks one that is due (expired, or no stale_after)
.TP
skogai memory\-stale(1)
entries that are due, oldest first, as name<TAB>stale_after<TAB>description; exit 1 if there are any
.TP
skogai memory\-new(1)
write a new entry from templates/entry.md; refuses an existing name
.TP
skogai memory\-index(1)
index lines for entries missing from the index, and index links to missing files. pure unless \-\-apply

exit 1 when something is out of sync and \-\-apply was not given.
\-\-apply appends the missing lines; dead links are only reported.
